{
  "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
  "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "jurisdiction come up when you were in the court of appeals?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Barry A. Short (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0000-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No trial has taken place, not at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Barry A. Short (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe that this Court, of course, has jurisdiction pursuant to section 1254 because it granted a writ of certiorari to the Eighth Circuit Court of Appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Barry A. Short (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government wants to forcibly administer to Dr. Sell antipsychotic drugs solely on the chance that it can, that it can bring him to trial on insurance fraud charges, nonviolent crimes. Dr. Sell does not want to be forcibly medicated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Then I wish you'd go back to a question I asked earlier that I don't think I got an answer to. What do you propose that we do with this man? He's been accused of a serious crime. For purposes of this case you're willing to assume it to be the same if he had been accused of a violent crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: He is -- his mental ability is such that he cannot be tried. The means are available to straighten his mind out so that he is competent to stand trial, but you say no, if he refuses that, we must respect his wishes. Then what do we do with him? Do we let him go?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: If he were found dangerous, he could be civilly committed. So here he is, nondangerous, but incompetent to stand trial. You -- you agree that civil commitment was -- isn't -- isn't available under those circumstances?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHORT: No, I -- civil commitment is what's going to happen to this individual under 4241."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHORT: He is subject to commitment under 4246."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He then has to make that certification. It goes to the district court. They have to prove that by clear and convincing evidence, and if they so show, he does remain committed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHORT: The standard, the standard, Your Honor, is whether or not -- and this is very basic, whether the person has the right to make the choice. Our position is that Dr. Sell has the right to make the choice over his medical decisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Riggins-style claim is clearly not amenable to review under the collateral order doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Harper-style claim is amenable to review under the collateral order doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0011",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The magistrate judge determined that the Government had not made a showing of dangerousness, which would have permitted medication under Washington v. Harper, but that it had adequately shown that medication was necessary in order to restore Dr. Sell to be competent for trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0001-0012",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: Well, at that point, Mr. Short is correct that under 4241 he would then be referred over to the director of a medical facility where he would be held for confinement to determine, pursuant to section 4246, whether, if released, he would be dangerous to himself or others."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: No, it's not obviously distinct, because I am assuming a person who is not a danger to himself or others is, in fact, in that position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: And it's not distinct because you say the Government has an interest in having him medicated for trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: He has not been getting antipsychotic medication."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2002-02-5664",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "11e4f4d37b572f086a18a761ee3494449a54ce287e6313371f5dff7489d92004",
      "evidence_id": "ev-11e4f4d37b57-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do not see any compelling interest whatsoever on the part of the Government in prosecuting this defendant, Dr. Sell."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
